"id": "section-1",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"shell text-column regional-guide\"><h2>Plumbing and electrical repairs in Perth Hills &amp; Swan Valley</h2><p>For Perth Hills and Swan Valley properties, include the suburb and any driveway, gate, site-contact or access detail that is relevant to the repair visit. Keep electrical, hot-water, drainage and leak symptoms separate.</p><h3>Plumbing repairs, drainage and hot water</h3><p>For Perth Hills and Swan Valley bookings, the repair request should connect the reported issue with the equipment location and practical site access. Our <a href=\"hot-water-problems-perth.html\">hot-water repair and replacement service</a> assesses the equipment, water connections and relevant electrical requirements, whether the unit is beside the home or in another accessible service area.</p><p>Visible moisture does not by itself identify a broken pipe. Our <a href=\"water-leak-detection-perth.html\">water leak detection service</a> investigates the affected area and explains any access work required to establish the source. For an active damaged pipe or connection, our <a href=\"burst-pipe-repair-perth.html\">burst pipe repairs</a> service addresses the reported water flow within the agreed repair scope.</p><p>Slow or backed-up fixtures are assessed through <a href=\"blocked-drains-perth.html\">blocked drain clearing and repair</a>. Describe which fixtures are affected and whether the symptoms are recurring. This page does not assume a particular drainage system, water source or property construction merely from the region name; the installation at your address determines the scope.</p><h3>Electrical repairs and installation</h3><p>Our <a href=\"power-faults-perth.html\">electrical fault finding and repair service</a> covers reported outages and faults in the property installation. Identify affected rooms or separate equipment areas from a safe position. We distinguish the fault being investigated from planned changes to lighting, outlets or equipment connections.</p><p>For recurring trips, request <a href=\"safety-switch-tripping-perth.html\">safety switch and RCD assessment</a> rather than repeatedly resetting the device. Let us know about visible water, damaged equipment or inaccessible service areas when booking. Do not enter a hazardous area, open covers or touch wet electrical equipment. Move clear and call 000 for immediate danger.</p><p>Work is carried out by appropriately licensed plumbing and electrical trades. Licence details are available on request. Our Perth team has an independent office and repair team within Ellis Services Group.</p><h2>Written quote before work proceeds</h2><p>Equipment location, access, existing connections and the confirmed fault affect the written quote. Investigation, repair and replacement options are identified separately, with additional pipework, cabling or access work described where required. No equipment package or system type is assumed before assessment.</p><p>Our team explains the recommended scope and written price before approved work proceeds. If findings require additional work, that change is discussed first. The handover records what was completed and any remaining item outside the approved scope, helping owners and managers plan the next step clearly.</p><h2>What to include in a repair request</h2><p>Include driveway, gate and on-site contact information relevant to the visit, plus the location of the affected equipment. If access to a separate building or locked service area is required, identify who can provide entry. These details support visit planning without asking you to inspect or test equipment yourself.</p><p>For a managed property, include the work order, occupant contact and approval pathway. Keep distinct faults as separate items, especially where plumbing and electrical work are both requested. Photos are optional and can be sent by email only when safely taken.</p><p>Call <a href=\"tel:0413477667\">0413 477 667</a> or <a href=\"contact.html\">request an on-site assessment and written quote</a>. You do not need to diagnose the fault before making contact.</p><h3>Suburbs within this service region</h3><p>Choose your suburb to prefill the property location in our contact form: <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Ellenbrook\">Ellenbrook</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Aveley\">Aveley</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=The%20Vines\">The Vines</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Henley%20Brook\">Henley Brook</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Brabham\">Brabham</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Caversham\">Caversham</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Swan%20View\">Swan View</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Stratton\">Stratton</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Jane%20Brook\">Jane Brook</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Bellevue\">Bellevue</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Greenmount\">Greenmount</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Darlington\">Darlington</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Mundaring\">Mundaring</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Kalamunda\">Kalamunda</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Lesmurdie\">Lesmurdie</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Gooseberry%20Hill\">Gooseberry Hill</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Walliston\">Walliston</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Pickering%20Brook\">Pickering Brook</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Parkerville\">Parkerville</a>, <a href=\"contact.html?suburb=Chidlow\">Chidlow</a>.</p><p>See <a href=\"service-areas.html\">all six Perth service regions</a> for our wider coverage.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
